---
import { PRODUCT_NAME, PRICE_NOW, PRICE_LATER } from '../../config';
import DocsLayout from '../../components/content/DocsLayout.astro';
---
<DocsLayout title="Licence and trial" description={`How the ${PRODUCT_NAME} trial and licence work: 14 days free, then one payment of $${PRICE_NOW} with lifetime updates.`} ogTheme="light">
  <p>Try {PRODUCT_NAME} free for 14 days, then buy it once. There is no subscription and no account to create.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Coming with the paid release.</strong> The trial and licence checks described here aren't in the current preview build yet. This page describes how they will work.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="trial">The 14-day trial</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The trial starts the first time you open {PRODUCT_NAME}. Every feature is included.</li>
    <li>You don't need to give an email address or card to start it.</li>
    <li>You can enter a licence key at any time during the trial or after it ends.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="buying">Buying</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>{PRODUCT_NAME} is a <strong>one-time payment of ${PRICE_NOW}</strong>, the launch price. It goes up to ${PRICE_LATER} later. See <a href="/pricing">pricing</a>.</li>
    <li>Every future update is included, for life. There are no renewals and no paid upgrades.</li>
    <li>Payment is handled by <strong>Polar</strong>, our reseller and merchant of record. Polar emails your licence key and receipt.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="activate">Activating your licence</h2>
  <p>Paste the key into {PRODUCT_NAME} and it is activated for that Mac. Activation needs an internet connection once. After that, {PRODUCT_NAME} checks the licence with Polar now and then when you're online. The check sends the key and an activation ID, never your code or repository data.</p>

  <h2 id="new-mac">Moving to a new Mac, or a lost key</h2>
  <p>To move your licence off a Mac you no longer use, or to find your key again, use the Polar customer portal. <a href="/licence">Licence help</a> walks through both, step by step.</p>
</DocsLayout>
